Lets the core's agent take accessibility actions in its tabs, which are hidden (#1625). Content
gives a WebContents the accessibility mode only while it isn't hidden, and a hidden one when it's
next shown, so a hidden tab's renderer never binds RenderAccessibility and
RenderFrameHostImpl::AccessibilityPerformAction drops the action unheard. An agent chooses an
option in a closed select through the option's kDoDefault, Blink's own path for a screen reader
(HTMLSelectElement::SelectOptionByAccessKey: no popup, and the page's input and change events as
a user's choice fires them), and its tab is in its own Space, never shown. A mode a scoper asked
for that WebContents alone now reaches it hidden too; the process-wide and profile-wide modes still
wait for it to be shown, as before.

diff --color -ruN a/content/browser/accessibility/browser_accessibility_state_impl.cc b/content/browser/accessibility/browser_accessibility_state_impl.cc
--- a/content/browser/accessibility/browser_accessibility_state_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/accessibility/browser_accessibility_state_impl.cc
@@ -777,8 +777,10 @@
     return;
   }
 
-  // Only update the WebContents if it is not hidden.
-  if (web_contents->GetVisibility() != Visibility::HIDDEN) {
+  // Only update the WebContents if it is not hidden, or if a scoper asked for this WebContents
+  // itself: the core's agent takes accessibility actions in its tabs, which are hidden.
+  if (web_contents->GetVisibility() != Visibility::HIDDEN ||
+      web_contents_mode.has_mode(ui::AXMode::kWebContents)) {
     web_contents->SetAccessibilityMode(effective_mode);
   }  // else the WebContents will be updated when it is revealed.
 }
